course: dictionary
lesson: 13940
title: Leprechauns and their clues
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A leprechaun comes from Irish folklore, which means old stories told in Ireland. You can work out what he is like from the clues around him. «The leprechaun wore a green coat and a tall green hat.» Green clothes and a little man's hat tell you he is a small, pretend character.
explain: «The mischievous leprechaun hid the teacher's chalk and giggled behind the door.» Mischievous means playful and naughty. The clues are hiding something and giggling, so a leprechaun is a little trickster, not a scary monster.
explain: «On St Patrick's Day we built a leprechaun trap out of a shoebox and gold paper.» A trap is something you make to catch an animal, so a leprechaun trap is built to catch a leprechaun. The clue St Patrick's Day shows it is a holiday craft.
explain: Always ask: could this happen in real life? A leprechaun is a figure from stories, not a real creature. If the words around him sound like a story, he is probably pretend.
fact: A leprechaun is a small, mischievous fairy from Irish folklore.
fact: Leprechauns are usually shown as little men with a red or ginger beard, a green coat and a green hat.
fact: In the stories, a leprechaun makes shoes and hides a pot of gold, often said to be at the end of a rainbow.
fact: In Irish folklore, if you catch a leprechaun he must grant wishes or show you his gold, but he is very tricky.
fact: Leprechauns are figures from stories, not real creatures.
exercise: «The leprechaun tipped his green hat and vanished before we could blink.» What does vanished mean? | Grew very tall | Fell fast asleep | *Disappeared suddenly | Shouted very loudly
exercise: What colour is a leprechaun's beard in the stories? | *Red or ginger | White | Blue | Black
exercise: «We built a leprechaun trap on St Patrick's Day.» Why would someone build a leprechaun trap? | *To try to catch a leprechaun in a holiday craft or story | To keep a real leprechaun warm | To hide the sun | To feed a real leprechaun
test: In Irish folklore, what must a leprechaun do if you catch him? | Turn into a bird and fly away | Tell you a joke | Hide in your shoe | *Grant wishes or show you his gold
test: What does mischievous mean? | Shiny and bright | Very tired and sleepy | *Playful and naughty | Kind and gentle
exam: Is a leprechaun a real creature? | Yes, but only on St Patrick's Day | Yes, they live in Ireland | *No, he is a figure from stories, not a real creature | Yes, you can see one in a forest
